ZkPassportMethodSetTrustedKeysTest
├── when the key admin sets eight valid words
│   ├── it should store the eight new words in order
│   └── it should emit TrustedKeysUpdated with the previous and the new words
├── when the key admin sets a zero guardian word
│   └── it should store the zero word
├── when the key admin sets a guardian word with only upper bytes set
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets seven words with a dirty address word
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should carry the length error
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets a non canonical version word
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets a version word with padding only in the first padding byte
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
└── when the key admin sets seven words with a non canonical version word
    ├── it should revert
    ├── it should carry the length error
    └── it should keep the previous words
